<title>GERMANY: Bonn to top up New Year bond by 2 bln dmk.</title>
<headline>Bonn to top up New Year bond by 2 bln dmk.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German government will top up its 10-year, six percent coupon New Year bond maturing on January 4, 2007 by a further two billion marks, raising the total volume of the issue to 30 billion marks, the Bundesbank as issuing agent said on Friday.</p>
<p>The additional volume will be placed from March 5 via German stock exchanges as part of the Bundesbank's market-smoothing operations, the central bank said.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
